```java
class Cat extends Animal {     // Cat genuinely IS-A Animal
    Cat(String name) { super(name); }
    @Override String sound() { return "Meow"; }
}
// Shared eat() reused; sound() specialized. IS-A test passes.
```
*If the IS-A test fails, prefer composition (HAS-A) instead of `extends`.*

```java
class Account {
    protected double balance;
    Account(double opening) { this.balance = opening; }
    void describe() { System.out.println("Balance: " + balance); }
}

class SavingsAccount extends Account {
    private final double rate;
    SavingsAccount(double opening, double rate) {
        super(opening);              // 1) call parent constructor (first stmt)
        this.rate = rate;
    }
    @Override void describe() {
        super.describe();            // 2) reuse parent's behavior
        System.out.println("Rate: " + rate); // then add more
    }
}
new SavingsAccount(1000, 0.04).describe(); // prints balance, then rate
```

